[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4774185386","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120558#issuecomment-4774185386","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120558","id":4774185386,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABHJBJqg","user":{"login":"BastiaanOlij","id":1945449,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDU0NDk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1945449?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij","html_url":"https://github.com/BastiaanOlij","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-22T23:50:54Z","updated_at":"2026-06-22T23:50:54Z","body":"Cool! I've been wanting to do this for some time now but never got around to doing it.\r\n\r\nOne thing I wanted to do differently is that instead of having the loop for views inside of `render_scene`, is to simply call `render_scene` for each eye if multiview wasn't available. It would result in a much more manageable diff. \r\nBut in true fashion of making things more difficult for myself, I also wanted to support the situation where  you would have more than a stereo result. So even with multiview support with 2 layers supported in our rendering engine, you could render to a 16 view texture in 8 steps (this would enable something like [looking glass](https://lookingglassfactory.com/) support).\r\n\r\nSo you'd end up with:\r\n```\r\nfor (int v = 0; v < view_count; v += max_views_per_pass) {\r\n  render_scene(...., v, min(max_view_per_pass, view_count - v));\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nWith `max_views_per_pass` being ` if multiview wasn't supported, and 2 if multiview is support. The two new parameters to `render_scene` being `p_start_view` and `p_num_views`.\r\nThat would have it's own set of consequences in making sure all the framebuffers were setup correctly and would in theory also require changes to the RD renderer to match.\r\n\r\nAnyway, food for thought. ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4774185386/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4779063337","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120558#issuecomment-4779063337","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120558","id":4779063337,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABHNq4KQ","user":{"login":"dsnopek","id":191561,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MTU2MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/191561?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek","html_url":"https://github.com/dsnopek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-23T12:13:51Z","updated_at":"2026-06-23T12:13:51Z","body":"> One thing I wanted to do differently is that instead of having the loop for views inside of `render_scene`, is to simply call `render_scene` for each eye if multiview wasn't available.\r\n\r\nI think that depends on how we want to think about this functionality.\r\n\r\nIf this is just \"multiview emulation\" for OpenGL/WebGL which may or may not have multiview support, then I think the way this PR does it is good, because it's fully contained within the compatibility renderer.\r\n\r\nHowever, calling `render_scene()` multiple times would mean moving the loop up into `RendererSceneCull` or  `RendererViewport`, which are used by all renderers. That could make sense if we wanted to use this functionality for more than just filling the gap when OpenGL/WebGL doesn't support multiview.\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4779063337/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4784406886","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120558#issuecomment-4784406886","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120558","id":4784406886,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABHSxBZg","user":{"login":"BastiaanOlij","id":1945449,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDU0NDk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1945449?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij","html_url":"https://github.com/BastiaanOlij","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-23T23:28:56Z","updated_at":"2026-06-23T23:29:23Z","body":"> > One thing I wanted to do differently is that instead of having the loop for views inside of `render_scene`, is to simply call `render_scene` for each eye if multiview wasn't available.\r\n> \r\n> I think that depends on how we want to think about this functionality.\r\n> \r\n> If this is just \"multiview emulation\" for OpenGL/WebGL which may or may not have multiview support, then I think the way this PR does it is good, because it's fully contained within the compatibility renderer.\r\n> \r\n> However, calling `render_scene()` multiple times would mean moving the loop up into `RendererSceneCull` or `RendererViewport`, which are used by all renderers. That could make sense if we wanted to use this functionality for more than just filling the gap when OpenGL/WebGL doesn't support multiview.\r\n\r\nYup, totally agree, and that is in a nutshell why I got stuck when I looked into this a little while ago as part of the viewport changes. The impact feels too large for an edge case.\r\n\r\nI just wanted to share it in case you thought you'd want to try and tackle the extra work, especially if we decide that we do eventually want to end up here.\r\n\r\nBut if we think this just isn't worth the effort, just adding this solution to take the pain away for OpenGL have spotty multiview support, that is a sound decision as well. ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4784406886/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5743977584","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120558#issuecomment-5743977584","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120558","id":5743977584,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABVl4kcA","user":{"login":"dsnopek","id":191561,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MTU2MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/191561?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek","html_url":"https://github.com/dsnopek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-19T17:36:34Z","updated_at":"2026-09-19T17:36:34Z","body":"I've rebased this one on https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123642 and changed it to disable WebXR Layers when multiview isn't supported, because there's really no sense in using WebXR Layers if we're not rendering with multiview, but this also has the nice side effect of making WebXR work out-of-the-box on Pico!","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5743977584/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5745821369","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120558#issuecomment-5745821369","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120558","id":5745821369,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABVnpGuQ","user":{"login":"dsnopek","id":191561,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MTU2MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/191561?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek","html_url":"https://github.com/dsnopek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-19T22:36:02Z","updated_at":"2026-09-19T22:36:02Z","body":"And with the latest changes in #123642 plus a couple small changes here, WebXR is now working on Apple Vision Pro too!","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5745821369/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5